    "message": "fix(skill): scope the PR to the skill and docs; drop the Compass monkey-patch\n\nNarrows this to the two pieces that belong in this repo — the `ix` agent skill\nand the HTTP API reference — and fixes the defects in what remains.\n\nRemoved, because the layer is wrong rather than the code:\n\n- `skills/ix/scripts/compass-patch/` — `apply.sh` string-injected a\n  `/__ix/remap` handler into the *compiled* `~/.ix/cli/cli/dist/cli/commands/\n  view.js` and regex-patched Compass's minified `KeyboardHelp-*.js`. This repo\n  owns `ix-cli/src/cli/commands/view.ts`, so that handler belongs in\n  `serverScript()` where it is typechecked, tested, and survives `ix upgrade`\n  instead of being overwritten by it. The handler also spawned `ix map` on an\n  unauthenticated POST, and `serverScript` calls `server.listen(PORT)` with no\n  host — binding 0.0.0.0, so it was reachable from the LAN and from any page in\n  the user's browser. `fit-view.js` wrote `canvas.style.zoom` and\n  `wrap.style.transform`, the two inline styles Compass drives from\n  `snappedZoom`/`snappedPan` state, so React restored its own values on the next\n  render; the 60ms re-apply timer was a race, not a fix. Its auto-frame also\n  duplicated Compass #57, which fixed the empty-first-paint upstream and ships\n  in v0.9.1.\n- `upstream/compass-fit-view/` — 723 lines of React that nothing in this repo\n  builds, typechecks or tests. It is a patch for another repo.\n\nBoth are preserved in this branch's history and are worth landing in\nsystem-compass, where the F-key fit view is genuinely new — Compass binds `0`\ntoday and nothing binds `F`.\n\nFixed in what stays:\n\n- `bootstrap.sh`'s `version_ge` was inverted. `sort -C` succeeds on ordered\n  input, so want-then-got asks \"want <= got\"; the `-r` asked the reverse. Node\n  22.22.2 against a floor of 22 warned \"requires Node >= 22\", and Node 18\n  passed silently. Verified across 22.22.2 / 24 / 22.0.0 / 20.11.1 / 18.4.0.\n- `install-skill.sh` unconditionally `rm -rf`'d `~/.claude/skills/ix` and\n  `~/.agents/skills/ix`. `ix` is a short name; a hand-written skill that\n  happened to share it was destroyed with no prompt, no backup and nothing in\n  the output. It now refuses unless the destination carries `name: ix`, with\n  `--force` to override.\n- `CLAUDE.md` carried `[redacted]/jacob/...`, a path from the author's machine, in\n  the file every agent in this repo loads. It also documented `dist/ix.zip` and\n  `.freebuff/run.md` as repo contents while gitignoring both.\n- `.gitignore`'s `dist/` was unanchored, matching at any depth; `/dist/`.\n- `docs/api/README.md` documented `POST /__ix/remap` as a real endpoint. It is\n  not one — a POST falls through to the SPA handler and returns index.html with\n  a 200, which the section now says.\n- `troubleshooting.md` had three rows whose remedies were the removed patch.\n\nThe `ix reset` is global and `registerPatchesCommand` is never registered\nfindings are kept — both verified, the second now tracked as #371.",
